TI  - Advances and prospects for the Human BioMolecular Atlas Program (HuBMAP).
PG  - 1089-1100
LID - 10.1038/s41556-023-01194-w [doi]
AB  - The Human BioMolecular Atlas Program (HuBMAP) aims to create a multi-scale 
      spatial atlas of the healthy human body at single-cell resolution by applying 
      advanced technologies and disseminating resources to the community. As the HuBMAP 
      moves past its first phase, creating ontologies, protocols and pipelines, this 
      Perspective introduces the production phase: the generation of reference spatial 
      maps of functional tissue units across many organs from diverse populations and 
      the creation of mapping tools and infrastructure to advance biomedical research.
CI  - © 2023. Springer Nature Limited.
